shackle and just bad. Like that was a nice building that was in my neighborhood and it had really nice columns on it and now it doesn't have any columns and the roof is falling down. And what nobody's going to do anything about that. They needed the equivalent of a Roman HOA, some enforcer who might keep up the standards of the neighborhood. And eventually, about 50 years after Constantine basically invented this kind of reuse, later emperors were passing laws trying to stop it.

